odQualityInteractionFile sizeCostRecommendation |       |       |              |                                               |                                |\n| --------------------------------------------------- | ----- | ----- | ------------ | --------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| Rive `.riv`                                         | 10/10 | 10/10 | Very small   | Free creation, export may require payment     | Best professional choice       |\n| Lottie `.json`                                      | 9/10  | 8/10  | Small        | Runtime free, creation may need After Effects | Good alternative               |\n| PNG sprite sheet                                    | 8/10  | 7/10  | Medium       | Free                                          | Best zero-cost option          |\n| APNG                                                | 7/10  | 3/10  | Medium/large | Free                                          | Simple looping only            |\n| Transparent WebM                                    | 9/10  | 4/10  | Large        | Free tools available                          | Cinematic animation only       |\n| GIF                                                 | 5/10  | 2/10  | Large        | Free                                          | Avoid for this mascot          |\n| Single PNG + CSS                                    | 5/10  | 5/10  | Very small   | Free                                          | Only floating/breathing effect |\n\nLottie is also suitable for Vue because it renders After Effects/Bodymovin animation JSON files on the web. [Official Lottie documentation](https://airbnb.io/lottie?utm_source=chatgpt.com)\n\n## My recommendation for your project\n\n### If your client wants a real interactive tiger\n\nUse:\n```css\nTiger artwork\n   ↓\nSeparate body parts\n   ↓\nRive animation\n   ↓\nVue profile page\n   ↓\nClick/touch changes animation state\n```\n\nThe tiger should be separated into:\n\n- &#x20;head&#x20;\n- &#x20;eyes&#x20;\n- &#x20;ears&#x20;\n- &#x20;body&#x20;\n- &#x20;arms&#x20;\n- &#x20;legs&#x20;\n- &#x20;tail&#x20;\n- &#x20;crown or accessories, if needed&#x20;\n\nA single PNG cannot independently blink, wave, move its tail, or open its mouth. It can only move, rotate, scale, float, or bounce as one complete image.\n\n### If you need a completely free solution\n\nCreate an 8–12-frame transparent PNG/WebP sprite sheet:\n```arduino\nidle-01\nidle-02\nidle-03\nblink\nidle-05\ntail-move\nidle-07\ncelebrate\n```\n\nThen animate it with CSS:\n```xml\n<template>\n  <div\n    class=\"tiger-mascot\"\n    role=\"button\"\n    aria-label=\"Animated tiger mascot\"\n    @click=\"playReaction\"\n  />\n</template>\n\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nfunction playReaction() {\n  // Change a class or trigger another animation here\n}\n</script>\n\n<style scoped>\n.tiger-mascot {\n  width: 110px;\n  height: 110px;\n  background-image: url('/mascot/tiger-sprite.webp');\n  background-repeat: no-repeat;\n  background-size: 800% 100%;\n  animation: tigerIdle 1s steps(8) infinite;\n  cursor: pointer;\n}\n\n@keyframes tigerIdle {\n  from {\n    background-position: 0 0;\n  }\n\n  to {\n    background-position: 100% 0;\n  }\n}\n</style>\n```\n\nThis is probably the best free method if you want to preserve the current tiger’s appearance closely.\n\n## Should you use transparent video?\n\nUsually, no—not for this profile page.\n\nTransparent WebM can create beautiful animation, but:\n\n- &#x20;the file is larger&#x20;\n- &#x20;interaction is limited&#x20;\n- &#x20;browser/device alpha support needs testing&#x20;\n- &#x20;controlling individual actions is more difficult&#x20;\n- &#x20;mobile loading may be slower&#x20;\n\nUse transparent WebM only if the tiger has a rich cinematic animation, such as jumping, dancing, or running across the screen.\n\n## How AI can help\n\nChatGPT/ImageGen can help create:\n\n- &#x20;matching tiger poses&#x20;\n- &#x20;idle, blink, wave, and celebration frames&#x20;\n- &#x20;a tiger character sheet&#x20;\n- &#x20;separate body-part artwork&#x20;\n- &#x20;animation design instructions&#x20;\n- &#x20;Vue/Rive/Lottie integration code&#x20;\n\nBut AI-generated animation frames may slightly change the tiger’s face, stripes, eyes, or proportions. For a client-facing mascot, use AI for references and assets, then clean and align the final frames manually in Rive, Krita, Photopea, or Figma.\n\nA practical workflow is:\n\n1. &#x20;Use the current PNG as the visual reference.&#x20;\n2. &#x20;Generate 6–12 matching poses with AI.&#x20;\n3. &#x20;Clean the images and align every frame.&#x20;\n4. &#x20;Export as a sprite sheet, Lottie, or Rive file.&#x20;\n5. &#x20;Let Vue control the position and click behavior.&#x20;\n6. &#x20;Keep the original PNG as a fallback for slow devices.&#x20;\n\n## Important clarification\n\nGit is not an animation format. Git stores and versions your files:\n```arduino\n/public/mascot/tiger.png\n/public/mascot/tiger-sprite.webp\n/public/mascot/tiger.riv\n/public/mascot/tiger.json\n```\n\nFor your specific profile page, my final choice is:\n\n- &#x20;Professional/client project: Rive&#x20;\n- &#x20;Free project: transparent WebP sprite sheet&#x20;\n- &#x20;Simple effect only: current PNG + CSS floating animation&#x20;\n- &#x20;Full cinematic tiger: transparent WebM video&#x20;","webApp-huwa3 ai for this project localhost test and then help me update the mascot of profile pages to animated mascot..","i wanted real animation real video likes animation or gif animation of this mascot tiger..","[https://editor.rive.app/home](https://editor.rive.app/home)\ncould ai using this app to help me create a animation waiving tiger, using mascot tiger here?&#x20;","[https://editor.rive.app/file/untitled/2578942](https://editor.rive.app/file/untitled/2578942)","i logged in continue","any more simplier? i could call ai chatgpt to use images  and direct call ai goes to which video generator website for free a