e flattened `currentInputImage` a destructive edit should build on, plus `originalUploadedImage` and `actionHistory` (each masked edit's current `mask.maskURI`, or `userRemovedMaskURI` if the user removed it).\n\n**WHEN TO USE THIS TOOL:**\n- Before a DESTRUCTIVE edit (e.g. `image_instruct_edit`, `image_generate`) that must build on the flattened result of prior non-destructive `interactive_*_app` edits, and only when you have no `outputUrl` from the previous tool. Call it, then pass the returned `currentInputImage` as the destructive tool's `imageURI`.\n- Before reusing a mask from an earlier edit, when no context is attached: the user may have edited or removed it in the editor. Pass the matching `actionHistory` entry's `mask.maskURI`. Reusing the same `mask.maskURI` across edits ties them together like a shared Photoshop layer mask: if the user later refines that mask in the editor, every edit sharing it moves to the refined mask. To target the same subject *independently*, generate a new mask instead — a fresh mask URL is treated as a separate mask.\n\n**DO NOT CALL THIS TOOL:**\n- Before a non-destructive `interactive_*_app` tool just to choose its image. Those stack on one base, so reuse the SAME `imageURI` you passed to the previous `*_app` edit (or the previous tool's `outputUrl`, or the freshly uploaded image) — NEVER `currentInputImage` or a rendition.\n- When the previous tool's response already contains an `outputUrl` — use that `outputUrl` directly as the next tool's `imageURI`.\n- When the session's editing context (`currentInputImage`, `originalUploadedImage`) is already attached to your context.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"sessionId":{"type":"string","description":"The widget-state session handle, unique to each source image (`originalUploadedImage`) — not one handle for the whole conversation. Set it to the `sessionId` a previous image tool returned for the image you are editing now. If that image has no `sessionId` yet (a newly u