rocessed image result.","type":"string"},"outputMediaType":{"description":"If tool succeeded, IANA media type of the asset at `outputUrl` (e.g. \"image/png\", \"image/jpeg\"). Set when the tool knows the output format deterministically; clients should prefer this over inferring from the URL or following redirects.","type":"string"},"requestId":{"description":"Request ID for tracking and debugging.","type":"string"},"originRequestId":{"description":"Diagnostic id of the call that started a long-running operation; every poll of that operation reports the same value. Quote it when reporting a problem. NOT a `taskId` — never pass it to a tool.","type":"string"},"success":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether the tool call was successful or not."},"importantNote":{"description":"Optional high-priority note for the assistant about this result: follow-up actions, caveats, or how to present or reuse the output.","type":"string"}},"required":["success"],"additionalProperties":{},"description":"A single item in the tool response (a tool may return several). Check `success` first: when true, use `outputUrl` or `outputFile` when present for the main deliverable; when false, use `error` for the error message. Always read `importantNote` if set, regardless of whether the call succeeded or failed."}}},"required":["results"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Output from MCP tool call"}},{"name":"adobe.markdown_to_pdf","title":"markdown_to_pdf","description":"Create a PDF from text/markdown written in the conversation. Does not require any file - takes the text directly.\n\nWHEN TO USE: \"turn these notes into a PDF\", \"make a PDF from this text\", \"create a PDF of what you wrote\", \"convert this markdown to PDF\", \"markdown to PDF\".\n\nCRITICAL: ALWAYS use this tool to create PDFs from text/markdown. NEVER write Python code (fpdf, reportlab, weasyprint, pandoc, etc.) to generate PDFs — this tool handles it with proper formatting and professional output.\n\nASYNC - this tool returns a tracking_id, NOT the final file. You MUST immediately call pdf_operation_status with the returned tracking_id and operation_name=\"markdown_to_pdf\" as your very next action. Do NOT tell the user the operation is processing. Do NOT stop your turn.\n\nWHEN NOT TO USE: To convert an existing file (Word, image, etc.) to PDF - use pdf_create instead.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"markdown_content":{"description":"Markdown text content to convert to PDF. This should be the raw markdown string from LLM chat conversations.","title":"Markdown Content","type":"string"}},"required":["markdown_content"],"title":"MarkdownToPDFInput"},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":false},"_meta":{"ui":{"resourceUri":"ui://widget/adobe-pdf-operations.html"},"resource_name":"adobe.markdown_to_pdf","_codex_apps":{"resource_uri":"/connector_69312da8e4dc81919370cb86fd172b6c/link_6abb1a24e0d88191bee88b0fb41f697e/markdown_to_pdf","contains_mcp_source":true},"connector_id":"connector_69312da8e4dc81919370cb86fd172b6c","connector_name":"Adobe","connector_description":"Design, combine, and edit","link_id":"link_6abb1a24e0d88191bee88b0fb41f697e","link_owner_profile":{}}},{"name":"adobe.interactive_image_remove_background_app","title":"Remove background","description":"**Session handle:** each source image (`originalUploadedImage`) has its own `sessionId`, minted on demand — it is not one handle for the whole conversation. The **first** call for a given source image must pass `sessionId: -1`; wait for the `sessionId` it returns and reuse that value for every later call on that same image. When `originalUploadedImage` changes to a different image, pass `-1` again to start that image's session, and keep a per-image mapping so returning to an earlier image reuses its `sessionId`.\n\nRemove background from your image and export with a transparent background in PNG format.\n\n**ROUTING — this widget owns every single-image request for background removal to a transparent cutout.** Count only the images this turn asks you to edit, not what the session holds.\n- **1 image this turn:** call THIS tool. Never ask widget-vs-server-side; never offer the direct tools (`image_remove_background`).\n- **2+ images this turn:** NEVER this tool — no batch form; use those direct tools and do not mention this one.\n- **1-image exceptions, use those direct tools when:** the user explicitly asks you to do it for them (\"just do it\", \"you pick\") — an explicit ask only, never inferred from terseness, a stated value, or impatience; a solid-color backdrop is wanted instead of transparency (`options.backgroundColor`).\n- **STOP after calling.** It renders its own result and returns no asset URL — no `asset_inline_preview`, `asset_preview_file`, `interactive_image_edit_preview`, or any next step.\n- **Non-generative** — never widens what generative editing is permitted.\n\n**Requires a mask:**\n- If no maskURI exists for this image, call image_select_subject_action_json tool first.\n- Verify the mask was generated from the same image being edited.\n- The mask required for this tool must be the background mask.\n   → If the mask is the subject mask, set toBeInverted to true.\n   → If the mask is the background mask, set toBeInverted to false.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"imageURI":{"type":"string","description":"The image to edit (accessible http/https URL). Choose by first match: (1) a new image uploaded with this request; (2) the previous tool's `outputUrl` if it just produced one; (3) the SAME `imageURI` you passed to the previous `*_app` edit — reuse it so consecutive effects stack on one base (a 2nd effect uses the 1st's input, NOT its result); (4) `originalUploadedImage`, the session's source image. NEVER use `currentInputImage` or any rendition — that is the flattened result and is for destructive tools only. Don't call `image_get_context` for this."},"originalUploadedImage":{"type":"string","description":"The source image this edit session is built on, and the key its `sessionId` is bound to. If an image was just uploaded to chat, use its reference; otherwise copy `originalUploadedImage` verbatim from the widget state of the image you are editing. It MUST stay constant while you keep editing the same image — NEVER set it to an edited, rendition, or tool-output image, which starts a new, empty history and loses prior edits. Each distinct `originalUploadedImage` has its own `sessionId`: whenever this changes to a different source image, pass `sessionId: -1` to start a new session for it."},"sessionId":{"type":"string","description":"The widget-state session handle, unique to each source image (`originalUploadedImage`) — not one handle for the whole conversation. Set it to the `sessionId` a previous image tool returned for the image you are editing now. If that image has no `sessionId` yet (a newly uploaded image, or you switched to a different one), set it to `-1`; a new handle is minted and returned — reuse that value for every later call on this image. Keep a `sessionId` per source image: returning to an earlier image reuses the handle from that image, not `-1`."},"mask":{"type":"object","properties":{"maskURI":{"type":"string","description":"The URI of the mask to be applied to the image. **Reusing a mask (only when the editing context with `actionHistory` is available):** the user can edit or remove masks in the editor, so a mask URL you passed earlier may be stale — the context's `actionHistory` lists each edit with its current mask. To carry a mask forward from an earlier edit, find that edit's most recent entry and pass its `mask.maskURI`, not the URL you originally passed; `isMaskUpdated` means the user edited it, so keep `maskDescription` / `toBeInverted` unchanged. If the entry has `userRemovedMaskURI` instead of `maskURI`, the user removed that mask: don't reuse it — call a selection tool if the request still targets that region, and pass `userRemovedMaskURI` only if the user explicitly asks for that mask again. To use the original AI selection instead of the user's edit, or after a crop, expand, straighten or undo-all, call a selection tool again. Use the attached context when present; call `interactive_image_get_context` only when none is attached."},"maskDescription":{"type":"string","description":"The description of what the mask is selecting."},"toBeInverted":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether the mask should be inverted, in order to select the inverted area."}},"required":["maskURI","maskDescription","toBeInverted"]},"replaceLastEdit":{"description":"Boolean value that tells the widget to undo the previous effect before applying the next requested.\n**For Example** a prompt like \"undo the last effect and apply a twirl\" would set this boolean to true to undo the last effect before applying what is requested in this prompt. With this input parameter the undoEdit tool does not need to be called before calling the next effect tool","type":"boolean"}},"required":["imageURI","originalUploadedImage","sessionId","mask"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false},"_meta":{"openai/outputTemplate":"ui://widget/pure-editor-carousel.html","openai/toolInvocation/invoking":"Removing background","openai/toolInvocation/invoked":"Background removed","ui":{"resourceUri":"ui://widget/pure-editor-carousel.html"},"resource_name":"adobe.interactive_image_remove_background_app","_codex_apps":{"resource_uri":"/connector_69312da8e4dc81919370cb86fd172b6c/link_6abb1a24e0d88191bee88b0fb41f697e/interactive_image_remove_background_app","contains_mcp_source":true},"connector_id":"connector_69312da8e4dc81919370cb86fd172b6c","connector_name":"Adobe","connector_description":"Design, combine, and edit","link_id":"link_6abb1a24e0d88191bee88b0fb41f697e","link_owner_profile":{}},"outputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-0