irment to use full, presigned urls rather than shortened urls (e.g. if this tool is being used to call out to external photoshop APIs that require a fully resolved URL without redirection)","type":"boolean"},"calledFrom":{"description":"The identifier of the component that called this tool","type":"string"},"sourceImageURI":{"description":"Fetchable URL (or data: URI) of the original source image this file was locally re-encoded from (e.g. a widget canvas re-export). Only honored when calledFrom is \"download-button\" or \"done-button\". When provided and the source carries a C2PA/content-credential manifest, the server re-signs the uploaded output to preserve provenance and reports metadata.caiPreserved=true.","type":"string"}},"required":["hasNextStep"]},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false},"_meta":{"ui":{"visibility":["app"]},"resource_name":"adobe.interactive_image_uploader_app","_codex_apps":{"resource_uri":"/connector_69312da8e4dc81919370cb86fd172b6c/link_6abb1a24e0d88191bee88b0fb41f697e/interactive_image_uploader_app","contains_mcp_source":true},"connector_id":"connector_69312da8e4dc81919370cb86fd172b6c","connector_name":"Adobe","connector_description":"Design, combine, and edit","link_id":"link_6abb1a24e0d88191bee88b0fb41f697e","link_owner_profile":{}},"outputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"results":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"description":"If failed, error message from the tool result.","type":"string"},"input":{"description":"Original input parameters passed to the tool","type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":{}},"metadata":{"description":"Optional metadata related to the tool result(s), will vary depending on the tool.","type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":{}},"originalURI":{"description":"Original input image URI, if applicable.","type":"string"},"outputFile":{"description":"If tool succeeded, the file object for the processed image result.","type":"string"},"outputUrl":{"description":"If tool succeeded, presigned URL for the processed image result.","type":"string"},"outputMediaType":{"description":"If tool succeeded, IANA media type of the asset at `outputUrl` (e.g. \"image/png\", \"image/jpeg\"). Set when the tool knows the output format deterministically; clients should prefer this over inferring from the URL or following redirects.","type":"string"},"requestId":{"description":"Request ID for tracking and debugging.","type":"string"},"originRequestId":{"description":"Diagnostic id of the call that started a long-running operation; every poll of that operation reports the same value. Quote it when reporting a problem. NOT a `taskId` — never pass it to a tool.","type":"string"},"success":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether the tool call was successful or not."},"importantNote":{"description":"Optional high-priority note for the assistant about this result: follow-up actions, caveats, or how to present or reuse the output.","type":"string"}},"required":["success"],"additionalProperties":{},"description":"A single item in the tool response (a tool may return several). Check `success` first: when true, use `outputUrl` or `outputFile` when present for the main deliverable; when false, use `error` for the error message. Always read `importantNote` if set, regardless of whether the call succeeded or failed."}}},"required":["results"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Output from MCP tool call"}},{"name":"adobe.font_search","title":"Search Fonts","description":"\nSearch the Adobe Fonts catalog for specific fonts.\n\nUse this to look up fonts by a free-form query and/or facets (foundry,\ndesigner, style, writing system), with sorting and pagination. For open-ended\n\"what font should I use for X\" design questions, prefer the font-recommendation tool.\n\n`user_query` and the facet filters (`foundry`, `designers`, `styles`,\n`moods`, `topics`, `font_group`, `writing_systems`, `exclude_variable_fonts`)\ncombine: the query is the search text and each facet narrows the\nmatches, so supplying more of them tightens the result set rather than\nbroadening it. The minimal call is a single `user_query` or one facet;\n`sort` orders the matches and `page`/`per_page` page through them.\n\nArgs:\n    user_query: Free-form text query (max 150 characters)\n    doc_type: Document type (e.g., 'postcard', 'Instagram post', 'movie poster')\n    styles: Comma-separated list of styles\n    moods: Comma-separated list of moods\n    topics: Comma-separated list of design topics\n    font_query: Set true when user_query is (or contains) a specific\n        font/family NAME the user wants to find (e.g. \"Acumin\", \"Minion\n        Pro\"), rather than a descriptive query. This performs a literal\n        name search: the matching family's styles are ranked to the top.\n        Leave false for descriptive/semantic queries.\n    text_hierarchy: Text focus ('heading' or 'body'); unrecognized\n        values are dropped and ignored rather than rejected\n    selected_font: PostScript name of a selected font for similarity\n    foundry: Comma-separated foundries to filter by\n    designers: Comma-separated designer names to filter by\n    library: Font library ('full' or 'trial'); unrecognized values\n        (e.g. 'adobe_fonts') normalize to 'full' rather than being\n        rejected. 'trial' is always honored as requested. 'full' is\n        clamped server-side to the caller's real Adobe Fonts\n        entitlement (via OAuth context, `bearer_token`, or a\n        server-configured fallback) — a free-tier caller\n        cannot widen their catalog by passing 'full'; with no\n        resolvable identity the effective value is 'trial'.\n    writing_systems: Comma-separated writing systems the results must cover, as ISO 15924 script codes (e.g. 'latn,cyrl' or 'hani'). Case, surrounding whitespace, common full names ('Latin', 'Korean', 'Chinese Simplified'), and BCP-47 tags ('zh-Hans', 'ja') are normalized to the closest supported script; unrecognized tokens are dropped, and an empty result falls back to 'latn' rather than being rejected. See this server's MCP instructions for the list of supported writing systems. Distinct from locale (which language names are translated into) and from supported_languages (a font's own language capability).\n    supported_languages: Optional list of language codes a returned font must support *all* of (AND semantics), via that font's language_support field. Case and separator variants ('zh_hans' -> 'zh-Hans', 'JA' -> 'ja') are normalized to the supported vocabulary; unrecognized codes are dropped rather than rejected, and if none remain no language filter is applied. Omit for no filtering. See this server's MCP instructions for the list of recognized language codes.\n    exclude_variable_fonts: When False (the default), variable fonts are\n        included in results alongside static fonts. Set True to omit\n        variable fonts entirely. There is no variable-only mode — this\n        only toggles whether variable fonts are included.\n    font_group: Comma-separated font groups (e.g., 'Sans Serif,Display')\n    sort: Result ordering ('relevance', 'name', or 'newest')\n    locale: Language the returned font family/style names (and\n        recommendation/search group names) are translated into, when a\n        translation is available (default en_US). Hyphen,\n        bare-code, and region-mismatched forms are all\n        normalized to the closest supported locale (e.g. ja-JP\n        and ja both become ja_JP; en_GB becomes en_US); an\n        unsupported value falls back to en_US rather than being\n        rejected. See this\n        server's MCP instructions for the list of supported locales.\n        Distinct from writing_systems (which script this call\n        matches against). Group/category names in the response are\n        localized only when the backend has a translation for the\n        resolved locale -- your value is normalized to its canonical\n        region-qualified form first, so passing a bare or hyphenated\n        code is fine; an untranslated group name silently falls back\n        to the default (English) name rather than erroring.\n    per_page: Number of results per page (default: 10)\n    page: Page number for pagination (default: 1)\n    bearer_token: Optional Adobe IMS access token, used only to resolve\n        the caller's real entitlement tier (see `library` above); usually\n        not needed when the MCP server's OAuth context already supplies one.\n\nReturns:\n    JSON string. On success: `{\"results\": [...], \"total\": <n>,\n    \"instructions\": <model guidance>}`. `total` is the full match count\n    (use `page`/`per_page` to page through it); `results` holds this\n    page's matches, either a flat list of font entries or a list of\n    groups each nesting its own `results` — walk it recursively to reach\n    the font entries.\n\n    Each font entry carries `font_identifier` ({postscript_name,\n    font_id}) when a font_id was resolved, or a bare `postscript_name`\n    when it could not; plus `family_name`, `style_name`, `full_name`,\n    `designers`, `foundry`, and `detail_url` (present when catalog\n    enrichment succeeded). Use them verbatim — never infer a\n    family/style/designer/foundry from a PostScript name, and omit a\n    detail when its field is absent. `font_identifier` (or the bare\n    `postscript_name`) is the chain key the rest of the suite consumes:\n    pass it as the one entry in a font_identifiers list into the\n    font-preview / font-details / font-styles / library-add / font-kit\n    tools. `preview_url`, when present, is a rendered specimen image\n    for your own inspection — fetch it to actually look at the font\n    before describing its appearance, rather than describing it from\n    the font's name or category. Never shown to the user (the\n    font-preview tool is how the user sees a font).\n    Each enriched font also carries `is_variable_font` (true/false). A\n    variable font additionally carries `axes` — a list of the axis tags\n    it exposes (e.g. `[\"wght\", \"wdth\"]`), tags only, deliberately no\n    min/max/default (only named instances are available, not the\n    true fvar table, so a range would be a guess); `axes` may be `[]`\n    for a variable font with no usable instances. Static fonts have\n    `is_variable_font` false and no `axes` key.\n\n    On failure, a business-error envelope `{\"error_code\": ...,\n    \"user_message\": ...}` — no `error` or `status_code` key — with\n    `error_code` \"invalid_input\" (input validation failed),\n    \"upstream_error\" (the lookup itself failed with a hard error), or\n    \"upstream_timeout\" (a transient failure — a timeout, connection error,\n    or 5xx; retrying may help).\n","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"user_query":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"title":"User Query"},"doc_type":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"title":"Doc Type"},"styles":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"title":"Styles"},"moods":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"title":"Moods"},"topics":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"title":"Topics"},"font_query":{"default":false,"title":"Font Query","type":"boolean"},"text_hierarchy":{"anyOf":[{"enum":["heading","body"],"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"title":"Text Hierarchy"},"selected_font":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"title":"Selected Font"},"foundry":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"title":"Foundry"},"designers":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"title":"Designers"},"library":{"default":"full","enum":["full","trial"],"title":"Library","type":"string"},"writing_systems":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":"latn","title":"Writing Systems"},"supported_languages":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"title":"Supported Languages"},"exclude_variable_fonts":{"default":false,"title":"Exclude Variable Fonts","type":"boolean"},"font_group":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"title":"Font Group"},"sort":{"default":"relevance","title":"Sort","type":"string"},"locale":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":"en_US","title":"Locale"},"per_page":{"default":10,"title":"Per Page","type":"integer"},"page":{"default":1,"title":"Page","type":"integer"},"bearer_token":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"title":"Bearer Token"}},"title":"search_fontsArguments"},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":false},"_meta":{"resource_name":"adobe.font_search","_codex_apps":{"resource_uri":"/connector_69312da8e4dc81919370cb86fd172b6c/link_6abb1a24e0d88191bee88b0fb41f697e/font_search","contains_mcp_source":true},"connector_id":"connector_69312da8e4dc81919370cb86fd172b6c","connector_name":"Adobe","connector_description":"Design, combine, and edit","link_id":"link_6abb1a24e0d88191bee88b0fb41f697e","link_owner_profile":{}},"outputSchema":{"properties":{"result":{"title":"Result","type":"string"}},"required":["result"],"title":"search_fontsOutput","type":"object"}},{"name":"adobe.log_analytics","title":"Log Analytics","description":"Logs analytics events from UI widgets.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"events":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"eventName":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the analytics event"},"properties":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"type":"string"},"description":"Event properties as key-value pairs"}},"required":["eventName","properties"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Array of analytics events to log"}