 present for the main deliverable; when false, use `error` for the error message. Always read `importantNote` if set, regardless of whether the call succeeded or failed."}}},"required":["results"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Output from MCP tool call"}},{"name":"adobe.image_get_task_status","title":"Wait for Operation","description":"Waits for an operation that a previous tool call started but did not finish, and returns its result once ready.\n\n**Use when:** any tool returned `status: \"working\"` together with a `taskId`. That result is NOT finished — there is no output yet — and this tool is the only way to get the real one.\n\nCall this with the `taskId` verbatim. If it comes back `status: \"working\"` again, the operation is still running: call this tool again with the `taskId` from the LATEST result. Usually that is the same value you sent, but for a batch it can be a new one — always use the most recent. Repeat until you get results.\n\nOne `taskId` may cover SEVERAL operations. It is then all-or-nothing: while any operation is unfinished you get a single `status: \"working\"` result with no outputs, and once they are all done you get every result together, in the order of the original request. You will never receive some of a batch's images now and the rest later.\n\nDo not report the operation as complete, and do not end your turn, until every result contains `outputUrl`.\n\nExample:\n    <example> Continue waiting: { \"taskId\": \"v1.aGVsbG8…\" } </example>","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"taskId":{"type":"string","pattern":"^v1\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,1024}$","description":"The `taskId` returned by a previous tool call whose result had `status: \"working\"`. Pass it back exactly as you received it.\n\nNever invent, construct, edit, or guess a value — it is opaque ciphertext, not a readable id, and a modified one is simply rejected. Only use a value some tool actually gave you."}},"required":["taskId"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":false},"_meta":{"resource_name":"adobe.image_get_task_status","_codex_apps":{"resource_uri":"/connector_69312da8e4dc81919370cb86fd172b6c/link_6abb1a24e0d88191bee88b0fb41f697e/image_get_task_status","contains_mcp_source":true},"connector_id":"connector_69312da8e4dc81919370cb86fd172b6c","connector_name":"Adobe","connector_description":"Design, combine, and edit","link_id":"link_6abb1a24e0d88191bee88b0fb41f697e","link_owner_profile":{}},"outputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"results":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"description":"If failed, error message from the tool result.","type":"string"},"input":{"description":"Original input parameters passed to the tool","type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":{}},"metadata":{"description":"Optional metadata related to the tool result(s), will vary depending on the tool.","type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":{}},"originalURI":{"description":"Original input image URI, if applicable.","type":"string"},"outputFile":{"description":"If tool succeeded, the file object for the processed image result.","type":"string"},"outputUrl":{"description":"If tool succeeded, presigned URL for the processed image result.","type":"string"},"outputMediaType":{"description":"If tool succeeded, IANA media type of the asset at `outputUrl` (e.g. \"image/png\", \"image/jpeg\"). Set when the tool knows the output format deterministically; clients should prefer this over inferring from the URL or following redirects.","type":"string"},"requestId":{"description":"Request ID for tracking and debugging.","type":"string"},"originRequestId":{"description":"Diagnostic id of the call that started a long-running operation; every poll of that operation reports the same value. Quote it when reporting a problem. NOT a `taskId` — never pass it to a tool.","type":"string"},"success":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether the tool call was successful or not."},"importantNote":{"description":"Optional high-priority note for the assistant about this result: follow-up actions, caveats, or how to present or reuse the output.","type":"string"},"status":{"description":"Whether the operation is still running (\"working\") or has finished (\"completed\"). When \"completed\", the deliverable is in `result`.","type":"string","enum":["working","completed"]},"taskId":{"description":"Present when `status` is \"working\": pass this exact value back to this tool to carry on waiting. Usually the id you supplied, but for a batch — where the set of unfinished operations shrinks each hop — it is a new one. Always send back the value from the most recent result, never an earlier one.","type":"string"},"statusMessage":{"type":"string","description":"Human-readable description of what the operation is currently doing. Safe to show the user as progress, but it is not a result — never treat it as one."},"pollInterval":{"type":"number","description":"Milliseconds to wait before calling `image_get_task_status` with this `taskId`. Normally 0: `image_get_task_status` blocks while it waits, so there is no reason to sleep first."},"result":{"description":"Present only when `status` is \"completed\": what the original tool would have returned. Read `result.outputUrl` for the deliverable — the surrounding object is an envelope, not a result.","type":"object","properties":{"success":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether the operation succeeded."},"outputUrl":{"description":"Presigned URL for the finished asset. The deliverable.","type":"string"},"outputMediaType":{"description":"IANA media type of the asset at `outputUrl` (e.g. \"image/png\").","type":"string"}},"required":["success"],"additionalProperties":{}}},"required":["success"],"additionalProperties":{}}}},"required":["results"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Output from MCP tool call"}},{"name":"adobe.acrobat_proxy","title":"acrobat_proxy","description":"Proxy for Adobe Document Cloud API calls with write/modify operations. This tool is for internal application workflows only. **DO NOT USE** this tool for any user-facing operations or general document processing workflows.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"url":{"description":"The complete URL to call. Must be from adobe.io or adobecontent.io domain. Can include query parameters, or provide them separately via query_params.","examples":["https://dc-api-stage.adobe.io/assets/123/actions"],"title":"Url","type":"string"},"method":{"default":"POST","description":"HTTP method to use. Default is 'POST'. Supported values: GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, PATCH","examples":["POST","PUT","DELETE"],"title":"Method","type":"string"},"body":{"anyOf":[{"additionalProperties":true,"type":"object"},{"items":{},"type":"array"},{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Request body. A dict or list is sent as JSON. A string is treated as a base64-encoded raw binary payload (e.g. for Content-Type: application/octet-stream, such as a C2PA/manifest signing payload) — it is decoded and sent byte-for-byte, with no JSON encoding.","examples":[{"action":"compress","parameters":{"level":"medium"}}],"title":"Body"},"headers":{"anyOf":[{"additionalProperties":true,"type":"object"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Additional HTTP headers to include in the request. The Authorization header with Bearer token is added automatically from the request context. Custom headers can override this if needed.","examples":[{"Accept":"application/json","Content-Type":"application/json"}],"title":"Headers"},"query_params":{"anyOf":[{"additionalProperties":true,"type":"object"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Query parameters to append to the URL","examples":[{"fields":"name,size","include":"metadata"}],"title":"Query Params"},"verb":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":